# Blue Hour

Dark Blue Hour is the primary appearance. A light theme uses the same semantic tokens.

Surfaces: background `#182B43`, sidebar `#203A57`, cards `#294967`, raised `#365A78`, ice panel `#DCECF3`, ink `#0B1E33`.

Accents, used sparingly: aqua `#42C8E8`, teal `#28C5B0`, mint `#8BE0B0`, lime `#C7E86B`, lavender `#B9AEFF`, amber `#FFC36B`, coral `#FF7D83`.

Aim for about 70% calm blue surfaces, 20% lighter slate or neutral surfaces, and 10% accent.

Manrope for headings and prominent rupee amounts. Inter for interface text. JetBrains Mono for meter readings and technical values. Noto Nastaliq Urdu for Urdu, loaded with `next/font/google`.

Glow is allowed only on a live forecast line or the main Cliff Guard gauge once that visualization is real. Do not glow buttons, cards, text, or decorative marks. Do not glow an unverified gauge.

No gradients used as decoration, no heavy glass, no neon styling, and no animation that does not explain a change.

Risk and trust chips always include a word and an icon. Do not communicate risk by color alone.
